<title>USA: Celadon buys 100 Freightliner trucks.</title>
<headline>Celadon buys 100 Freightliner trucks.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS, Ind. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Celadon Group Inc said Wednesday it purchased 100 truck tractors from Freightliner Corp, a Portland, Oregon-based unit of Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
<p>Delivery of the vehicles is scheduled from January through May 1997.</p>
<p>The purchase is part of the company's $28 million capital program for fiscal 1997. Celadon's current fleet consists of 1,200 tractors and 4,300 trailers.</p>
<p>Celadon is a truck-load company specializing in the transport of goods to and from Mexico.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk, 312 408-8787</p>
